      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was renamed Viola after the daughter of a local landowner, replacing its original name Canterbury Station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Viola_Delaware",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The station quickly became a commercial hub, shipping farm produce like peaches and receiving supplies that fueled local growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
